flowchart TB
  accTitle: Yazi shortcuts grouped by task
  accDescr: Group the Yazi 26.9.1 default shortcuts into navigation, search, file operations, and tabs. Copy or cut first, navigate to the destination, and press p to paste. Trash and permanent deletion are shown separately.

subgraph navigation["Navigation and search"]
    direction TB
    move["Move up/down: j / k or arrow keys<br/>Enter directory: l<br/>Go to parent: h"]
    jump["Top: g → g; bottom: G<br/>o / Enter invokes the opener"]
    search["Search: /, type a keyword, Enter<br/>Next match: n; previous match: N"]
    hidden["Toggle hidden files<br/>. (period)"]
    move ~~~ jump ~~~ search ~~~ hidden
  end
  subgraph files["Files and tabs"]
    direction TB
    transfer["Copy: y; move: x<br/>Navigate to the destination, then p"]
    edit["Create: a; rename: r<br/>End a new directory name with /"]
    select["Select: Space; select all: Ctrl+A<br/>Trash: d; permanently delete: D"]
    tabs["New tab: t → t; close tab: Ctrl+C<br/>q quits the entire application<br/>Switch: 1 / 2 / 3<br/>Previous/next tab: [ / ]"]
    transfer ~~~ edit ~~~ select ~~~ tabs
  end
